    rationale: The source expressly conditions Retirement Allowance on prior REA, without equating the two
      benefits.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol11-ch71/0125
      quote: "71778   A person who ceases to be entitled to REA is entitled to RA for life if on the day\n     \
        \   before it ceased there was entitlement to REA at a rate of £2.00 or more per week\n                \
        \                    1\n        (from one or more awards) . If the assessment of IIDB ceases from a date
        after the\n        award of RA starts entitlement to RA continues.\n                                   \
        \                                         1 SS CB Act 92, Sch 7, para 13(2) & (3)"
